  "title": "An abelian Lie triple system makes counting polynomial in every class",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "for p odd, N of exponent p and class c < p with an involution theta and n = n+ + n- (Lazard): [[n-, n-], n-] = 0 iff every odd Lie word of degree at least 3 in n- vanishes iff n- + [n-, n-] is a subalgebra with [n-, n-] central in it; and then, for every group pi with H^1(pi; F_p) = H^2(pi; F_p) = 0 and every psi: pi -> C2, |Hom_psi(pi, N x| C2)| = |Z^1(pi; F_p^psi)|^(dim n-), every homomorphism landing in exp(n- + [n-, n-]) x| <theta>. Hence counting maps to N x| C2 is polynomial on closed 3-manifolds with H1(M; F_p) = 0 and bounded 2-rank, in every class; with H1 = Z/2 the count is 1 + p^((N+1) dim n-).",
